(n)
"Inter-Se-Merit" means the order of merit declared by the Competent Authority in respect of various classes or category
of Candidates ;
(o)
"JEE Main" means the Joint Entrance Examination conducted by the Central Board of Secondary Education, New Delhi
for the concerned academic year ;
(p)
"Minority Quota" means seats earmarked for the Minority Community students from within the State, belonging to the
Minority Community to which the institution belongs ;
(q)
"Non-Autonomous Institution" means those institutions which are not `Autonomous Institutions' ;
(r)
"OHU" means the area Outside Home University area ;
(s)
"Overseas Citizen of India (OCI)" means a candidate or a person registered as an Overseas Citizen of India as declared
by the Central Government under section 7A of the Citizenship Act, 1955 and includes Persons of Indian Origin (PIO) ;
